  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Selgantolimod and Inter-alpha-trypsin inhibitor heavy chain H1, mediated through the compound Magnesium levulinate. This is supported by multiple paths indicating that Selgantolimod targets different entities, including Keratin, Nucleoside diphosphate kinase A, and Plasma kallikrein, all of which are targets of Magnesium levulinate. The shared pathway involving Magnesium levulinate as a common target suggests a possible mechanism of action where Selgantolimod may influence the activity of Magnesium levulinate, which in turn affects the Inter-alpha-trypsin inhibitor heavy chain H1. The consistent scores across the three paths (final_score=0.7153) indicate a strong level of confidence in the observed relationships, though the exact nature of the interaction between Selgantolimod and Magnesium levulinate remains to be elucidated. The evidence supports a functional link between Selgantolimod and the Inter-alpha-trypsin inhibitor heavy chain H1, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction.",
